- the social card image (og.png)

What is code, and therefore MIT instead
--------------------------------------

- the site shell (index.html), stylesheets, page modules and data files as
  software
- the build, check and test scripts under dev/

You can tell the two apart in practice: if you want to reuse the *text* of a
topic, CC BY-NC-SA applies; if you want to reuse the *engine* that renders it,
MIT applies.

If you reuse the content
------------------------

- **credit**: name the atlas ("CS Atlas") and link back to the page you used
- **non-commercial**: no use that is primarily intended for commercial advantage
  or monetary compensation — no ad-supported republishing, no paid courses or
  books built from it, no bundling into a paid product
- **share alike**: anything derived from this content must also be
  CC BY-NC-SA 4.0
- say what you changed, if you changed it

Short quotes with a link back do not need to follow the share-alike clause; it
applies when you republish substantial portions.

